{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-78a24a4a492ba26d4560","statement":"(i) We have a canonical isomorphism\n\n$$\\on{H}^*(\\Gr(i,n))\\cong \\wedge^i (\\bigoplus_{j=0}^{n-1}\\Ql[-2j](-j)).$$\n\n(ii) Let $X_n\\subset \\bP^{n+1}$ be the smooth $n$-dimensional quadric. Then\n\n\\[\n\\on{H}^*(X_n)\\cong\\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\bigoplus_{j=0}^n \\Ql[-2j](-j) &  n \\mbox{ is odd,} \\\\\n\\bigoplus_{j=0}^n \\Ql[-2j](-j)\\bigoplus \\Ql[-n](-\\frac{n}{2}) &  n \\mbox{ is even.}\n\\end{array}\\right.\n\\]\n\nThe proof is by identifying $\\Gr(i,n)$ and $X_n$ as minuscule Schubert varieties of $\\on{PGL}_n$, $\\on{SO}_{n+2}$.","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"4024e668b370e0111f726608231a1259966bc9b8549c712962db1d7c662f509a","kind":"example","label":"Example 171","ref_key":"","name":"","order":205,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":2885,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":511,"math_hints":56}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","macros":{"on":"\\operatorname","fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakl":"{\\mathfrak l}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","frakq":"{\\mathfrak q}","fraks":"